abstract: >-
  Curated publication-derived summary tables, reconstruction and consistency
  verification code, source provenance, and explicit reproducibility limits for
  a chemical mass balance source-profile-choice study. The archive preserves
  the released 21-file publication-derived package and adds scoped licensing,
  citation metadata, and current verification instructions. The checks reproduce
  reported summary arithmetic; they do not independently rerun the original
  source-native JRC or EPA CMB fits or establish environmental allocation accuracy.
  Private Fairbanks materials, third-party source binaries, the manuscript, and
  journal submission documents are excluded. CC BY 4.0 applies to author-owned
  data/documentation, and MIT applies to original software as specified in
  LICENSE_SCOPE.md; third-party rights are not relicensed.
keywords:
  - chemical mass balance
  - source apportionment
  - source profiles
  - fit diagnostics
  - publication-derived data
  - consistency verification
